`renderLoading` is now defined inside the component body and passed as a prop to `<WebView renderLoading={renderLoading}>`. Previously it was defined outside the component and was stable. Since it now depends on `styles`, wrap it in `useCallback` to avoid creating a new function reference on every render:

```tsx
const renderLoading = useCallback(() => (
    <View style={[StyleSheet.absoluteFill, styles.fullScreenLoading]}>
        <ActivityIndicator
            size={CONST.ACTIVITY_INDICATOR_SIZE.LARGE}
            reasonAttributes={{context: 'WalletStatementModal'}}
        />
    </View>
), [styles.fullScreenLoading]);
```
